  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "Octal radix converters count leading zeros in the 10-digit limit, check places first, and reject logicals with #VALUE!",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, OCT2BIN, OCT2DEC, and OCT2HEX reject whitespace and leading signs with #NUM!, reject logical arguments with #VALUE!, count leading zeros toward the 10-character input limit (so OCT2BIN(\"00000000000\") is #NUM!), and treat 10-character octal inputs whose high bit (2^29) is set as 30-bit two's-complement negatives. OCT2BIN and OCT2HEX validate an explicit places argument (truncating into 1..=10) before inspecting number.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in jnt_w111_rounding (Excel 16.0.20527.20088) and build 20430 witness sets; matched 100% of full-bank rows (OCT2BIN 1,201/1,201, OCT2DEC 2,060/2,060, OCT2HEX 1,198/1,198) and 120/120 pinned rows each.",
